Here's the full program targeting `net11.0`:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var person = new Person("Alice", 30);

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
};

string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string name, int age);
```

**Output:**
```
{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}
```

The key is `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` — a built-in naming policy that converts property names to PascalCase. Since your record uses lowercase parameter names (`name`, `age`), this policy capitalizes the first letter of each word in the JSON output.
